  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given NNN intervals where the ithi^{th}ith interval is [Li,Ri][L_i,R_i][Li​,Ri​].\n\nIn one operation, you will:\n\n\nChoose an integer MMM (1≤M≤N)(1 \\leq M \\leq N)(1≤M≤N) and select MMM **distinct** indices x1,x2,…,xMx_1,x_2,\\ldots,x_Mx1​,x2​,…,xM​.\nFor the ithi^{th}ith selected index xix_ixi​ (corresponding to range [Lxi,Rxi][L_{x_i},R_{x_i}][Lxi​​,Rxi​​]):\n\nChoose an integer KiK_iKi​ where (1&lt;Ki≤(Rxi−Lxi+1))(1 \\lt K_i \\leq (R_{x_i}-L_{x_i}+1))(1&lt;Ki​≤(Rxi​​−Lxi​​+1));\nPick KiK_iKi​ **distinct** integers Y(i,1),Y(i,2),…,Y(i,Ki)Y_{(i,1)},Y_{(i,2)},\\ldots,Y_{(i,{K_i})}Y(i,1)​,Y(i,2)​,…,Y(i,Ki​)​ from the range [Lxi,Rxi][L_{x_i},R_{x_i}][Lxi​​,Rxi​​].\n\n\nWe define the following for an operation:\n\n\nThe cost is defined as the product of all KiK_iKi​. Formally, cost =∏i=1MKi= \\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^M K_i=i=1∏M​Ki​\nThe score is defined as the product of all picked integers over all chosen intervals.\n\nFormally, score =∏i=1M∏j=1KiY(i,j)= \\displaystyle\\prod_{i=1}^M \\displaystyle\\prod_{j=1}^{K_i}Y_{(i,j)}=i=1∏M​j=1∏Ki​​Y(i,j)​.\nAn operation is good if:\n\n\nMaximum number of intervals are chosen.\n\nIn other words, the value of MMM is the maximum possible.\nThe cost of the operation is **not greater** than NNN;\nYour task is to find the **sum** of scores of all possible good operations  mod   998244353\\bmod\\;998244353mod998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN, the number of intervals.\nFollowing NNN lines contain two space-separated integers each, Li,RiL_i,R_iLi​,Ri​, describing the interval.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **sum** of the scores of all possible good operations  mod   998244353\\bmod\\; 998244353mod998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Li&lt;Ri≤1091 \\leq L_i \\lt R_i \\leq 10^91≤Li​&lt;Ri​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
